{
  "ticket": "t-opt-paired",
  "_droppable": false,
  "_role": "spec",
  "_what": "T13 interleaved PAIRED measurement of optimization-3 (occl table vs DDA). T12 failed because arms ran in configuration CLUSTERS and session drift (~15 FPS between identical configs) swamped the effect. Here arms strictly alternate c,d within each pair so the paired difference cancels common drift. Sessions: PN = near geometry (legacy 2.5/6), PF = far geometry (!synth N 32, closer to the real remote-light case with longer DDA paths).",
  "_arm_order": "STRICT interleave: inside every pair the two arms are adjacent (c then d). Noise reference = two IDENTICAL c8 arms placed first and last in the session (pair=noise). Never reorder the arms of a session.",
  "_analysis": "Per pair i: dX_i = FPS(c_i) - FPS(d_i) (positive = occl ON slower = no table benefit); benefit B_i = -dX_i. Report paired median, per-pair signs, D_adj (adjacent identical pair) and D_span (session-spanning identical pair). NEVER compare cross-arm medians (exactly the T12 failure). Tools: tools/paired-analyze.ps1.",
  "_sensitivity": "TWO noise references. (a) ADJACENT identical-config pair (pair=anoise, pn10-c8x/pn10-c8y, back-to-back): D_adj = |FPS(x)-FPS(y)| = the WITHIN-PAIR noise scale the paired test faces -> this is the primary threshold X = max(D_adj, 1.0). (b) SESSION-SPANNING identical-config pair (pair=noise, pn00-c8 first vs pn99-c8 last, and pf00/pf99 far): D_span = the drift scale that T12 let swamp its result; reported for contrast, NOT used as the threshold. Inference: pairing cancels common drift, so dX = FPS(c)-FPS(d) has residual ~ single-arm 3s-window noise; the median of n=5 paired differences has SE ~ 1.253*sigma/sqrt(5) ~ 0.56*sigma, and D_adj is an empirical upper bound on sigma, so X = max(D_adj,1.0) is conservative. Sign test: 5/5 same sign is p ~ 0.031 one-sided. If |paired median| < X, report the effect as below the rig noise floor X FPS at that geometry -- an effective negative, never \"unmeasurable because the fixture failed\".",
  "_leverage": "Far geometry (!synth N 32) moves the lights 32 blocks ahead aimed parallel-forward -> much longer per-sample DDA march -> where the table can actually win. Near geometry keeps DDA paths short and can mask the effect.",
  "_conversion": "total ssbo count = 2 (self handheld + gun) + N (!synth N); far arms are !synth 6 32 = same count 8, distance 32.",
  "_judgment": {
    "paired_median_positive": "optimization-3 benefit readable at that geometry",
    "paired_median_below_threshold": "effective NEGATIVE result: in this scene the table-vs-DDA benefit is below the rig noise floor X FPS",
    "noise_pair_large": "session drift still large -> more pairs / shorter session",
    "far_vs_near": "effect only in PF => the T12 null was a DDA-path-length artefact, not a product bug"
  },
  "_min_decisive": "PN noise pair + PN n1..n5 (12 arms), then PF fnoise + f1..f5 (12 arms). n6..n8 control and n9/f6 tm-off cross-checks are trimmable.",
  "_run": "powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\\opt-verify-taclight.ps1 -Spec tickets\\t-opt-paired.json -Session PN -BenchReps 3 -BenchWarmup 1 -Evidence ...\\qa5\\run-out-PN  (then -Session PF, same 800p setup)",
  "_prereq": "Window 1280x800; client restarted after compileJava syncShaderPack (fixture gained the optional !synth distance). Run tools/check-synth-spec.ps1 first. Arms must not be reordered.",
  "scoped": "window 1280x800 (options.txt fullscreen:false + override 1280x800) / dev save test / scene wall / pose wall_front(2000.0,121.5,8.0,yaw180,pitch5) / midnight+clear+doMobSpawning false / wait 20 / single client + !synth fixture / relay !bench x3 (3s) median = PRIMARY / ticket bench = SECONDARY",
